{"name":"Prunus Avium","hex":"#dd4492","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"prunus","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of traditional decoration on porcelain that depicts the leaves and branches of the Chinese plum, Prunus mume."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prunus"}],"entries":[{"title":"Prunus avium","blocks":[{"text":"Prunus avium, commonly called wild cherry, sweet cherry or gean, is a species of cherry, a flowering plant in the rose family, Rosaceae. It is native to western Eurasia and naturalized elsewhere. It is an ancestor of P. cerasus."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Prunus_avium_fruit.jpg/330px-Prunus_avium_fruit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prunus_avium"},{"title":"Prunus","blocks":[{"text":"Prunus is a genus of flowering trees and shrubs from the rose family (Rosaceae) that produce stone fruits, or drupes. As of March 2024, the genus has about 340 accepted species, including almonds, apricots, cherries, peaches, and plums. It has a cosmopolitan distribution, being native to the temperate regions of North America, the neotropics of South America, and temperate and tropical regions of Eurasia and Africa."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Fr%C3%BChling_bl%C3%BChender_Kirschenbaum.jpg/330px-Fr%C3%BChling_bl%C3%BChender_Kirschenbaum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prunus"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/01_Prunus_sp..jpg/500px-01_Prunus_sp..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/01_Prunus_sp..jpg/1280px-01_Prunus_sp..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wiki